export anchor FestivalLineupStyle:
    number: 94
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Festival lineup
    idea: The dashboard printed as a music festival lineup poster, with projects billed on stage columns, headliners sized by how many tasks they carry, and set times for the team's activity.
    base: light
    palette:
        cream: #fff4e3, the poster paper and the page
        nightInk: #22102e, all text, rules and the primary button
        smoke: #4a3a52, meta lines and day labels
        stageTeal: #0d5c63, week one bars, On track and links
        magenta: #b3165f, week two bars, act progress bars, stage tags and nav stars
        sirenRed: #a3122a, Behind and overdue
        amberInk: #8a4b00, At risk
        sun: #f6b93b, the sunburst behind the brand and the focus glow, never text
        lilac: #ecdcf5, the box office bar and empty progress tracks
    type:
        Display is a condensed heavy sans, Avenir Next Condensed, Roboto
        Condensed, Arial Narrow, sans-serif at 800 with font-stretch
        condensed, always uppercase. Text is system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto,
        sans-serif. The brand is 56 to 150px fluid caps at 0.85 line height,
        the greeting 34 to 64px caps, summary numbers 64px, headliner names
        48px, then 36, 28 and 22px by task count, section bills 34px, body
        15px at 1.5 and labels 12px caps tracked 0.14em.
    layout:
        A slim lilac box office bar holds a Box office tag, the search field,
        New project, the bell with a count and the user. Below it a centred
        poster head has the date and presents line, the huge brand over pale
        sun rays fanning from a half sun, and caps nav links split by
        magenta stars. The greeting is centred with a red outlined warning
        box. The four numbers sit in one band between 3px ink rules, split
        by hairlines. The lineup has three stage columns, Engineering, Design
        and Research, and Marketing, each with two acts centred under a 3px
        rule, the bigger project billed larger, with meta, a magenta progress
        bar, percent and status. Below, a bar chart called Fourteen nights
        sits beside Set times, a list with the time in magenta caps and the
        person in condensed caps. Stages stack below 900px and the numbers
        go two by two on phones.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px gutters between stage columns and 48 to 56px between bands.
    density: Medium. Big type up top and tighter fine print lower down, like a poster.
    corners: Square everywhere except the round avatar and notification count.
    borders: 3px ink rules over each stage and around the numbers band, 1px ink rules between acts and set times.
    shadows: None. Depth comes from the sunburst behind the brand.
    icons:
        Solid shapes in currentColor at text size. A filled circle for On
        track, a filled triangle for At risk and a heavy cross for Behind and
        overdue, always with the caps word. Stars divide the nav.
    focus: A 3px ink outline offset 2px inside a 7px sun yellow glow.
    tone: Festival billing in caps, such as The lineup, Fourteen nights, Set times and Tonight's warning.
